 {"id": "DF-0924-07", "title": "P1 --auth-file without --auth=apikey silently serves EVERYTHING UNAUTHENTICATED (no key, wrong key, and garbage key all return 200/201) — the flag implies 'this daemon is locked to this store' but does nothing on its own; DF-0919/DB-GAP-043 hardening made the file load fatal but not the enforcement", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-09-24T12:05:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T12:05:00Z", "reasoning": "Dogfood 2026-09-24 measured on scratch daemon :3795 started as 'node bin/duckbrain.js http --port=3795 --auth-file=<store>' (no --auth flag): (1) GET /api/memories with NO X-API-Key header -> 200 full data; (2) POST /api/memories with NO key -> 201 created; (3) GET with X-API-Key: wrongkey -> 200. The auth store parsed fine (fatal on missing/unparseable works — DB-GAP-043 good) but the middleware is never mounted without --auth=apikey. Same-shaped trap as DF-0924-01 class: an operator who sets --auth-file believes the daemon is locked. Fix direction: when --auth-file/duckbrain_AUTH_FILE is provided, either auto-enable apikey auth or fail startup with 'auth-file requires --auth=apikey'; at minimum log a loud WARNING banner at boot. Fix: src/cli/http.ts createHttpServer auth resolution"}
